{
  "id": "ss.relic.camo",
  "name": "Dead leaf",
  "description": "A dead leaf with legs: a whole brown leaf, rib and veins and stalk, and three jointed limbs folded out from under one side of it. Nothing about the leaf is faded or unfinished — earlier passes drew it giving out halfway along, on the idea that the ability is not being found and an unfinished object says so, but a leaf that stops being a leaf is a broken drawing before it is a clever one, and at 32px the soft end was mud. The camouflage is carried by the joke instead: it is a leaf until you notice it has legs, which is the whole of what the relic does to the swarm. The limbs are outlined and painted a tone up from the plate — at carapace-dark they were dark on dark and gone by 32px, and legs you cannot see at icon size turn this back into a plain leaf. They are bent once each, because a jointed limb reads as a leg where a straight bar reads as a twig, and a twig is the one thing this must not be mistaken for.",
